## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design with privacy considerations in data-labeling.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence and lineage
- Cross-tenant lifecycle with SLAs
- API for CAPA creation/update with logs/traces and policy links
- Privacy metrics: exposure window, recurrence rate
- RCA template and canary rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal CAPA type
class CAPARecord {
  constructor(id, evidence, lineage, owners) {
    this.id = id; this.evidence = evidence; this.lineage = lineage; this.owners = owners;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify exposure window in MTTI terms?
- What telemetry would you add to prove recurrence reduction after rollout?

## Why This Is Asked

Gauges ability to design end-to-end CAPA artifacts for data exposure in multi-tenant data platforms.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data modeling
- Lifecycle state machines
- API design for incident records
- Telemetry and tenant-scoped metrics
- RCA templates and Canary remediation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal REST handler sketch for creating a CAPA
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => {
  const { cap_id, incident, tenant_id, evidence } = req.body;
  if (!cap_id || !tenant_id) return res.status(400).send('Missing fields');
  // store CAPA entry
  res.status(201).json({ cap_id, status: 'created' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the CAPA under concurrent backup runs?
- What metrics would you monitor to ensure containment over time?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a robust, auditable CAPA for external data sources, focusing on provenance, containment speed, and reproducibility of fixes in a multi-source pipeline.

## Key Concepts

- External data provenance and signatures
- Drift detection and automated containment
- CAPA data model: evidence, lineage, owners
- Metrics for containment, recurrence, and verification
- RCA templates and canary rollback planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: verify feed signature before ingestion
function verifySignature(feedPayload, signature, key) {
  const h = crypto.createHmac('sha256', key);
  h.update(feedPayload);
  return h.digest('hex') === signature;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle revocation of compromised feeds without delaying normal ingestion?
- What audits or reports would you expose to satisfy regulatory or governance needs?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design practical CAPA governance tied to real-time data flows and multi-tenant risk without overengineering.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model fields (id, tenant_ids, sink, data_classification, evidence, region, remediation_links, state)
- Region-aware lifecycle states
- Minimal REST API (POST /caps, PATCH /caps/{id})
- Metrics: recurrence_rate, MTTR, false_positives, containment_time per region
- RCA template and safe-canary rollback plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express endpoints for CAPA creation
const app = require('express')();
app.use(express.json());
app.post('/caps', (req, res) => { /* create CAPA */ res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123' }); });
app.patch('/caps/:id', (req, res) => { /* update CAPA */ res.status(200).send({ ok: true }); });
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end CAPA design for a real multi-tenant data routing bug with data residency risk, ensuring traceability from detection to verification and rollback.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, tenant IDs, and route metadata
- Region-aware lifecycle state machine with clear escalations
- Linked logs/traces in CAPA records for auditability
- Canary rollout and RCA templates with measurable metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal REST API skeleton for CAPA creation
app.post('/capa', (req, res) => {
  const { evidence, tenantId, routeInfo } = req.body;
  // persist CAPA and link logs/traces
  res.status(201).send({ id: 'capa-123', status: 'open' });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify false positives and tune thresholds across regions?
- What automated checks would prevent reintroduction of the misrouting in future deployments?

